{% extends "_base.md.j2" %}
{% block body %}
You are the Leader triaging a task, before any work starts.

This turn is read-only: make no edits to the repository or the trackers.

Decide:
- `mode`: `implement` for a self-contained change, `plan` when a plan turn should shape the
  work first, including when the request needs decomposing into several tasks, as it does
  when it spans several tracker entries: each entry becomes its own task. An open
  decision is not a reason to plan: a plan turn cannot raise it, while an implement task
  raises it through consult to you and, if you cannot decide it, to the Operator.
- `complexity`, `acceptance_criteria` and `references`.

When the request has an acceptance-criteria section, carry its bullets into
`acceptance_criteria` unchanged. The section starts at a line holding only one of
`## {{ acceptance_criteria_heading }}`, `{{ acceptance_criteria_heading }}:`,
`**{{ acceptance_criteria_heading }}**` or `**{{ acceptance_criteria_heading }}:**`, in any
letter case.
{% endblock %}
